<title>USA: Alco Standard Corp Q4 net rose.</title>
<headline>Alco Standard Corp Q4 net rose.</headline>
<dateline>VALLEY FORGE, Pa. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except earnings per share)</p>
<p>				    Three Months Ended September 30</p>
<p>						 1996	1995  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues				$1,124,708   860,124   30.8%</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations   43,814     30,395  44.1</p>
<p> Discontinued operations		 11,131     16,683</p>
<p> Net income				  54,945     47,078</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share</p>
<p> Continuing operations		     0.30	 0.20   50.0%</p>
<p> Discontinued operations		   0.08	 0.14</p>
<p>						   0.38	 0.34</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	   131,953    117,706   12.1%</p>
<p>					 Fiscal Year Ended September 30</p>
<p> Revenues				$4,099,773   3,091,602  32.6%</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations   164,893    115,011  43.4</p>
<p> Discontinued operations		  45,848     88,661</p>
<p> Net income				  210,741    203,672</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share</p>
<p> Continuing operations			1.12	 0.86  30.2%</p>
<p> Discontinued operations		    0.36	 0.76</p>
<p>						    1.48	 1.62</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	    127,649    116,474   9.6%</p>
<p>NOTES: 1995 amounts restated for fiscal 1996 poolings.</p>
<p>Per share after payment of preferred dividends of $4.9 million vs $6.5 million in quarter and $23.3 million vs $15.2 million in year.</p>
<p>First Call consensus estimate for Q4 was $0.45 per share.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
